# Scenario diag-stic2-mob-pass (plan 08-07, D-04, D-05, D-10): outcome pass, exit 0. The program ivs-diag-stic-2 through the
# project boot stub contract 2 with the zero graphics ROM and KEY_1 closed from tick 0: the first read of 01FE returns the low
# byte 7E, so the program shows the three moving-object scenes in turn (scene 1 in frames 1 to 3, scene 2 in frames 4 to 6,
# scene 3 from frame 7). The asserts are the hand-derived expectations of data/golden/diag-stic2-mob-pass.expect (derivation in
# docs/video/diag-stic-2-derivation.md, section (f), written before the program): the same lines in the same order as the
# committed block of that document, and the same as the .expect (golden-expect-drift). The idle control diag-stic2-idle-pass
# differs from this scenario in the video and input digests only (data/expected/scenario-pairs.ids). KEY_1 is applied at tick 0,
# before the program's read, and the asserted frames are one frame or more from every scene change. It never halts.
ivss 1
id diag-stic2-mob-pass
profile intv-2609-ntsc-family-p1
content exec boot-stub-2
content grom zero-grom
content cart diag-stic-2.ivsc
capture video 0 10
input at_tick=0 c0=KEY_1 c1=0x0
run-to 640000 ticks
assert halted == no
assert mem 02F0 == 03C5
assert mem 02F1 == 000A
assert mem 02F2 == 007E
assert mem 02F3 == 0003
assert frame 0 displayed == no
assert frame 2 displayed == yes
assert frame 8 displayed == yes
assert frame 2 hash == a00823f4684b712a38cfdf239e93a63d8f585a58526f568e38b4156148d07b43
assert frame 5 hash == 222a489123b6c1e16cf56eaf93d58d6c2ae7e6a2c52024ef1dfe26e0e2b8f8d2
assert frame 8 hash == 4d249118cfb21b13b05f961cb1d273e47c7ab713249fef197fdd5a7d0191159e
assert frame 2 pixel 150 90 == 4
assert frame 2 pixel 152 90 == 1
assert frame 2 pixel 158 95 == 4
assert frame 5 pixel 38 24 == 4
assert frame 5 pixel 64 24 == 5
assert frame 5 pixel 118 38 == 6
assert frame 8 pixel 24 28 == 5
assert frame 8 pixel 24 36 == 4
assert frame 8 pixel 76 48 == 9
assert video count == 10
